  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep veggies: Finely chop the onion. Discard the husk and silks from the corn. Slice the corn kernels from the cob. Finely chop the zucchini. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Crumble the stock cubes into a large heatproof jug, add 625ml (2½ cups) boiling water and stir to dissolve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/244267/photos/large/prep_veggies-7bb6a162834f4d2bfc018d9ccf89a213.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soften onion: Pour 1 tbs oil from the marinated goat cheese into a medium saucepan and heat over medium heat. Cook the onion and garlic, stirring occasionally, for 3 mins or until softened. Add the rice and corn and cook, stirring, for 1 min or until well coated.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/244268/photos/large/soften_onion-fab631035c43cade7de531edd02826ca.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook risotto: Add the stock to the pan, bring to the boil, then reduce the heat to low and cook, covered, for 15 mins. Stir in the zucchini and cook, covered, for 5 mins or until most of the liquid is absorbed and the rice is almost tender. Remove from the heat. Stand, covered, for 5 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/244269/photos/large/cook_risotto-494a0f433ba890dc2e3f762d997d4396.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add spinach: Add the spinach to the risotto and stir until wilted. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/244270/photos/large/add_spinach-bdc64ac632f7a50fc47a1e2968005a61.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the risotto among bowls. Coarsely chop the goat cheese, scatter over the risotto and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/244271/photos/large/serve_up-edefba3fb5d037435a5db69cdf7f25e1.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: If your little ones aren't keen on goat cheese, simply leave it out of their portion and replace with grated cheddar or parmesan if you have some on hand.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/244272/photos/large/make_it_yours-6d30fd53d6d3771f2e87f834b1569a78.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
